<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maryland County</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> County is the south-easternmost county of Liberia, on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Côte d'Ivoire</a>, with its capital at Harper. It covers the territory of the former Republic of Maryland, founded by African American settlers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-palmas">Cape Palmas</a>, which was annexed to Liberia in 1857 after a war with the Grebo. Its economy rests on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a>, farming and fishing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maryland-county.jpg" alt="Maryland County" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Derivative work: User:Profoss *Original work: Uwe Dedering · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maryland_in_Liberia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
